cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this workflow repository, please cite it together with the underlying methods and dataset papers."
title: "Donor-held-out reference mapping of the Human Heart Cell Atlas with scVI, scANVI, and scArches"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-21
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/USERNAME/heart-atlas-reference-mapping"
url: "https://github.com/USERNAME/heart-atlas-reference-mapping"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible donor-held-out reference-mapping case study on the 20k-cell
  subsampled Human Heart Cell Atlas shipped with scvi-tools. One complete donor
  is held out as an unseen query, scVI/scANVI are trained on the remaining
  donors, and scArches query mapping is used to transfer labels. Query labels
  are sealed until predictions are frozen. A PCA + kNN baseline and a
  confidence-coverage analysis are included. This is an educational adaptation
  of published workflows, not a reproduction of the scArches paper and not a
  new biological study.
keywords:
  - single-cell
  - scRNA-seq
  - reference mapping
  - scArches
  - scVI
  - scANVI
  - human heart cell atlas
  - label transfer
authors:
